From 7ced54b497b0ed5dee295b7ae71ef000a5a42311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:11:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: why HDR is not told, the colour of the
 video, pictures dropped and skipped

Data that the overview page needs and that the player did not give:

- why the display is not told that an HDR video is HDR: the reason that
  CHDRSignal already finds and writes to the log (no property on the
  connector, no EDID, no HDR in it, not this EOTF, no blob, not queued), and
  now also that HDR is off in the display settings, where SetHDR() returned
  before it found anything. Kept as a number (HdrNotSentCode()) for the
  player information to read from its own thread;
- what the video says of itself when SetHDR() is given its picture: its
  primaries, transfer function and range, with "assumed" where the stream
  said no primaries and Kodi chose them by the size of the picture
  (VideoPicture::m_originalColorPrimaries is what the stream said), its
  matrix, its mastering display and its light levels. Formatted once for
  each video, not once for each frame;
- the pictures that the video player dropped and that its renderer skipped
  (the "drop" and "skip" of its debug line, which no label gave), written
  into the data cache by the video thread each time it updates its
  information.
---
 xbmc/cores/DataCacheCore.h                  | 12 ++++
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp |  5 ++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp         | 72 +++++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h           | 25 +++++++
 4 files changed, 114 insertions(+)

